From: SN Fast Sync <snfast@localhost.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:39:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(snjs,web): optional fast polling, off unless switched on
 (1 s default, 0.5 to 3 s)

Hosted Standard Notes gives the desktop and mobile apps no push channel, so a change on another device waits for the next
30 s auto sync tick. With the owner's switch on, the app in front syncs every second instead (configurable 0.5 to 3 s;
a window that is not focused, a hidden window and the background keep the 30 s tick). The tick stays quiet while a websocket is
open, while a sync runs, while the sync frequency guard is tripped and for one minute after a failed sync (HTTP 429, no network).
Switch: localStorage "snfast.fastPolling" = "1" or window.snfastSetFastPolling(true, { intervalMs, unfocused }).

